.TH RUNVPN 8 "October 2026" "runvpn 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
runvpn \- start, stop and restart an openconnect VPN connection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B runvpn
.BR start | stop | restart
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B runvpn
is a small wrapper around
.BR openconnect (8)
that connects to the VPN server configured in
.IR /etc/runvpn.conf ,
reading the password from the clipboard.
.PP
The command must run as root: when started by a normal user it runs itself
again through
.BR sudo (8).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start
Read the password from the clipboard, clear the clipboard and start
.B openconnect
in the background.
Fails if the clipboard is empty or if the VPN started by
.B runvpn
is already running.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the
.B openconnect
process started by
.BR runvpn ,
waiting up to 10 seconds for it to exit.
Other
.B openconnect
processes are not touched.
.TP
.B restart
Stop the VPN and, if it stopped, start it again.
The password must be copied to the clipboard again.
.SH CLIPBOARD
The clipboard is read as the user who invoked
.BR sudo .
On Wayland
.BR wl-paste (1)
is used when installed, otherwise
.BR xclip (1)
reads the X11 clipboard.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/runvpn.conf
Configuration file. Sets
.B VPN_SERVER
(the VPN server address) and
.B VPN_USER
(the VPN username).
.TP
.I /etc/sudoers.d/runvpn
Lets members of the
.B runvpn
group run
.B runvpn
without a password.
Add a user with
.BR "adduser <user> runvpn" .
.TP
.I /run/runvpn.pid
PID of the
.B openconnect
process started by
.BR runvpn .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
on error: missing configuration, empty clipboard, VPN already running,
VPN not stopped or wrong arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo runvpn start
sudo runvpn stop
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openconnect (8),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR xclip (1),
.BR wl-paste (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Nicola Danese <nicola.danese@e-projectsrl.it>
